# Manjula deployment rules for Cursor

Before modifying Docker, CI/CD, Kubernetes, Cloudflare, runners, health checks, ports, release tags, or production topology, read:

- `docs/DEPLOYMENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `AGENTS.md`
- `CLAUDE.md`
- `.github/workflows/staging-image.yml`
- `.github/workflows/promote-gitlab.yml`

## Implemented now

- GitHub is source of truth.
- YOGA-5090 is staging/regression.
- Regression port 18081; persistent UAT port 18080.
- UAT URL: `https://staging.manjulab.com`.
- Build once on YOGA-5090, then promote exact tested artifact.
- GitLab production release project: `KAI-Production / Hosted Customers / Manjula / website-release`.
- Immutable promotion tag: `release-<short-sha>`; moving pointer: `approved-latest`.
- GEEKOM primary: candidate 18083, production 18082, Caddy 8080, Cloudflare origin `geekom-web-origin.kai247.com`.
- gpuserver DR: K3s namespace `brahmando`, deployment `manjulab-web`, container `web`, origin `india-web-origin.kai247.com`.
- Both gpuserver probes must use `/healthz`.
- Production jobs are manual and dedicated-runner only.
- No rebuild occurs after UAT approval.
- Promotion opens a GitLab pipeline over the API with `MANJULA_*` release variables; it hands off and never deploys.

## Roadmap, not current behavior

Do not assume these exist yet:

- digest-pinned `@sha256:` runtime deployment;
- automatic public-origin health gates;
- automatic Worker failover regression on every release;
- guaranteed Windows-side WSL auto-start;
- formal release retention/rollback catalog;
- production rollout of the new logo.

## Never do

- never rebuild on GitLab/GEEKOM/gpuserver after UAT;
- never reuse port 18080 for regression;
- never restore `/index.php` probes;
- never reintroduce old Apache/PHP command/args/mounts;
- never use non-idempotent JSON Patch remove operations for optional old fields;
- never route production to shared/hosted runners;
- never expose secrets or runner tokens;
- never introduce paid Cloudflare Load Balancing unless explicitly requested.

If live infrastructure conflicts with the documented architecture, stop and surface the discrepancy instead of inventing a topology.
